I've read the full test file, the project file, the .NET extension, and the extended 19-smell catalog. Here's the formal audit.

---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest v4.1.0 · .NET 10 · Integration-test calibration applied
**Taxonomy:** [testsmells.org](https://testsmells.org/) 19-smell catalog (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| Critical | 1 | 1 |
| High | 1 | 1 |
| Medium | 2 | 2 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4 of 8** |

Half the tests (4 of 8) are clean and well-structured. The other 4 each carry a distinct smell.

---

### Critical

#### 1. Unknown Test (Assertion-Free Test) — `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ⚠ No assertion — passes even if every insert silently fails
}
```

**Risk:** This test inflates pass counts and coverage while verifying nothing. If `Insert` began silently dropping rows, this test would still pass.

**Fix:** Assert on the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### High

#### 2. Conditional Test Logic — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 101)

```csharp
var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)     // ⚠ one branch may never run
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Risk:** Since `Insert(new User(...))` creates a standard `User`, the `PremiumUser` branch will never execute. The `DiscountRate` assertion is dead code that gives false confidence in `PremiumUser` coverage.

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests, each with a known type:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### Medium

#### 3. Sleepy Test — `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // ⚠ 3-second wall-clock sleep
```

**Risk:** Adds 3 seconds to every CI run, and the delay may not be long enough on slow agents (flaky) or may be far too long locally (wasted time). The method is also marked `async Task` but never uses `await`, generating compiler warning CS1998.

**Fix (integration-calibrated):** Replace with a polling loop with a timeout:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var notified = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(notified, "Notification was not sent within timeout");
}
```

> **Integration-test calibration note:** In pure unit tests this would be **High**. Downgraded to **Medium** because the class is explicitly `[TestCategory("Integration")]` and the test covers real async notification behavior.

#### 4. Assertion Roulette — `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);           // no message
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);    // no message
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email); // no message
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);       // no message
```

**Risk:** When one assertion fails the MSTest runner reports a line number but no semantic context. With 4 assertions and no messages, failure diagnosis requires opening the file.

**Fix:** Add messages describing the business expectation:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "Inserted user should be retrievable by email");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should survive round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should survive round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

---

### Smells Not Detected (15 of 19 clean)

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite — no external resource coupling |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | Each test exercises one logical operation |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | All numeric literals (3, 10, 100) are self-documenting from context |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `ToString()`-based comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` in tests |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` annotations |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No identical assertion repeated |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests sharing `Insert`/`GetByEmail` cover distinct behaviors |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Clean | Proper `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` lifecycle |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is meaningful |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` / `Debug.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No `Assert.IsTrue(true)` tautologies |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | Schema created in setup, no assumptions on pre-existing state |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All methods have executable code (the *assertion-free* issue on `BulkInsert` is tracked as Unknown Test above) |

---

### Positive Observations

- **`sealed` test class** — MSTest 4 best practice, prevents accidental inheritance
- **Clean AAA structure** in 5 of 8 tests — arrange/act/assert phases are clearly separated
- **Good naming convention** — `Method_Scenario_Expected` throughout
- **Proper resource cleanup** — `[TestCleanup]` disposes the SQLite connection
- **Hermetic fixtures** — each test gets a fresh in-memory database, no ordering dependency
- **`[TestCategory("Integration")]`** correctly applied

---

### Prioritized Remediation

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|------------|--------|
| 🔴 1 | Unknown Test (`BulkInsert`) | ~2 min — add one assertion | Eliminates false-confidence coverage |
| 🟠 2 | Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser`) | ~10 min — split into two tests | Removes dead branch, gains real `PremiumUser` coverage |
| 🟡 3 | Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert`) | ~10 min — add poll helper | Faster CI, eliminates flakiness risk |
| 🟡 4 | Assertion Roulette (`InsertUser`) | ~2 min — add message strings | Better failure diagnostics |
